The routers' lease, keep-alives and `wait_before_close` (#1011's item 3;
observer §5.2). Five judgements read a window by them: `check conform`,
`alarms`, `telemetry`, `timing` and `arbitration`; and so does an
`alert-firing` rule under `watchdog` and `record --on`. None of the three is on
the bus, and a tool's own session configuration states only its own pushes'
wait, so each verb takes the deployment's word, most specific first:

1. `--lease` and `--wait-before-close`, each where given;
2. `--face-policy`'s `[transport]`, which the routers run (`link.v2` §2.16);
3. the defaults of the zenoh `--binding` names (`link.v2` §2.19):
   `zm-1.10.2-r1` waits 10 s before it closes a transport, `zenoh-1.10.1` 5 s;
4. zenoh 1.10.1's.

One rule resolves them for every verb (`cmd::zk2::routers`), before any
session opens. The cases below run on a dead bus (`connect.timeout_ms: 0`),
so a run that reaches the session read its flags without complaint.

## `--binding` on each verb

```console
$ zenctl check conform lab/meter meter.v1 --binding zm-1.10.2-r1 --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5
? 2
Error: failed to open the Zenoh session

Caused by:
    Unable to connect to any of [Single(tcp/127.0.0.1:1)]!
check conform: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

$ zenctl alarms --binding zm-1.10.2-r1 --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5
? 2
Error: failed to open the Zenoh session

Caused by:
    Unable to connect to any of [Single(tcp/127.0.0.1:1)]!
alarms: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

$ zenctl telemetry --binding zm-1.10.2-r1 --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5
? 2
Error: failed to open the Zenoh session

Caused by:
    Unable to connect to any of [Single(tcp/127.0.0.1:1)]!
telemetry: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

$ zenctl timing --binding zm-1.10.2-r1 --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5
? 2
Error: failed to open the Zenoh session

Caused by:
    Unable to connect to any of [Single(tcp/127.0.0.1:1)]!
timing: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

$ zenctl arbitration --binding zm-1.10.2-r1 --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5
? 2
Error: failed to open the Zenoh session

Caused by:
    Unable to connect to any of [Single(tcp/127.0.0.1:1)]!
arbitration: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```

## `--binding` on `watchdog` and `record --on`

Two more verbs build a window's reader: an `alert-firing` rule reads
alarms.v1 as `alarms` does, under `watchdog` and under `record --on`. Neither
takes `--lease` or `--wait-before-close`, so each is told its routers' zenoh
by `--binding`, through the same rule. No other rule reads it. Their
`--face-policy` is the face a raw observer reads across (`--across-face`),
where no `alert-firing` rule is asked.

```console
$ zenctl watchdog --rule 'alert-firing zk2/** warning' --count 1 --binding zm-1.10.2-r1 --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5
? 2
Error: failed to open the Zenoh session

Caused by:
    Unable to connect to any of [Single(tcp/127.0.0.1:1)]!

$ zenctl record -o /dev/null --on 'alert-firing zk2/** warning' --pre 5 --binding zm-1.10.2-r1 --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5
? 2
Error: failed to open the Zenoh session

Caused by:
    Unable to connect to any of [Single(tcp/127.0.0.1:1)]!

```

`record --binding` is the triggered form's, as `--clocks-synced` is: without
`--on` it is refused, exit 2.

```console
$ zenctl record 'zk2/**' -o /dev/null --binding zm-1.10.2-r1
? 2
error: the following required arguments were not provided:
  --pre <SECS>
  --on <RULE>

Usage: zenctl record --out <FILE> --pre <SECS> --on <RULE> --binding <NAME> --namespace <NS> <SELECTOR>...

For more information, try '--help'.

```

A binding is one of `link.v2` §2.4's names. Any other is refused, exit 2,
with the names it could have been.

```console
$ zenctl timing --binding zenoh-1.10.2
? 2
error: invalid value 'zenoh-1.10.2' for '--binding <NAME>': not a binding; one of: zenoh-1.10.1, zm-1.10.2-r1

For more information, try '--help'.

$ zenctl watchdog --rule dropped --binding zenoh-1.10.2
? 2
error: invalid value 'zenoh-1.10.2' for '--binding <NAME>': not a binding; one of: zenoh-1.10.1, zm-1.10.2-r1

For more information, try '--help'.

```

## `--face-policy` on `timing` and `arbitration`

The routers' `link.v2` face policy, as `check conform` and `alarms` take it:
its `[transport]` states every key, so it stands over `--binding`, and a flag
over it.

```console
$ zenctl timing --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/media/rf.face.toml --binding zm-1.10.2-r1 --lease 20 --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5
? 2
Error: failed to open the Zenoh session

Caused by:
    Unable to connect to any of [Single(tcp/127.0.0.1:1)]!
timing: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

$ zenctl arbitration --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/media/rf.face.toml --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5
? 2
Error: failed to open the Zenoh session

Caused by:
    Unable to connect to any of [Single(tcp/127.0.0.1:1)]!
arbitration: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```

A `link.v1` policy states no transport. It is refused, exit 2, before any
session, by every verb alike.

```console
$ zenctl timing --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/radio.face.toml
? 2
Error: --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/radio.face.toml: a link.v1 policy states no transport: leave it out and give --binding, or --lease and --wait-before-close, or give a link.v2 policy (link.v2 §2.16)
timing: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

$ zenctl arbitration --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/radio.face.toml --binding zm-1.10.2-r1
? 2
Error: --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/radio.face.toml: a link.v1 policy states no transport: leave it out and give --binding, or --lease and --wait-before-close, or give a link.v2 policy (link.v2 §2.16)
arbitration: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

$ zenctl alarms --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/radio.face.toml
? 2
Error: --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/radio.face.toml: a link.v1 policy states no transport: leave it out and give --binding, or --lease and --wait-before-close, or give a link.v2 policy (link.v2 §2.16)
alarms: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

$ zenctl check conform lab/meter meter.v1 --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/radio.face.toml
? 2
Error: --face-policy ../examples/zk2/link/radio.face.toml: a link.v1 policy states no transport: leave it out and give --binding, or --lease and --wait-before-close, or give a link.v2 policy (link.v2 §2.16)
check conform: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```

A flag that is no positive number of seconds is refused the same way.

```console
$ zenctl arbitration --wait-before-close 0
? 2
Error: --wait-before-close must be a positive number of seconds, got 0
arbitration: the question could not be asked — exit 2, the reserved non-verdict (1 here would claim a verdict this run never reached)

```
